Uploads on macOS - william@william.co.il 03.2025 (Updated for modern macOS)

This script uploads files with a random filename, original filename in a random subfolder, or packaged as RAR or ZIP (with encryption if desired).
- If run on a directory, it automatically packages it as ZIP (default) or RAR.
- Directories are packaged relative to their parent folder, keeping the archive clean without leaking absolute system paths.
- By default, the URL is automatically copied to the clipboard without trailing newlines.
- Passwords are automatically generated (using pwgen or secure native macOS /dev/urandom fallback) and saved locally in ~/.upl.
- Works natively on macOS 10.15 through macOS 15+ (Sequoia) on both Apple Silicon and Intel Macs.

Automator Workflows / Quick Actions:
- Screenshot: Interactive area screenshot capture, instant upload, and clipboard copy.
- Upload: Upload selected files/folders from Finder right-click context menu.
- Upload File or Folder - Encrypted: Upload with random password encryption.
- Upload File or Folder - Original Filename: Preserve original filename in a random remote subfolder.
- Notifications work out-of-the-box using native macOS Notification Center banners (no external notifier required).

Switches:
-h / --help              - This help output
-c / --cli               - CLI mode for shell/script usage: prints only the URL (and password) to stdout or exits with code 1
-i / --input             - File or directory to upload (full or relative path; quotes recommended)
-s / --server            - Target server config to use (default: server1)
-nc / --nocopy           - Do not copy URL to clipboard, only output to terminal
-o / --original          - Keep original filename in an isolated remote subfolder
-p / --package           - Enable packaging (automatically enabled for directories)
-e / --encrypt           - Encrypt package with a generated 32-character password
-cp / --copypassword     - Copy password after URL into clipboard (default: enabled)
-ncp / --nocopypassword  - Do not copy password into clipboard
-nsp                     - Do not save password to local password file (~/.upl)
-rar                     - Use RAR format instead of ZIP (default: ZIP)
-t / --tmpdir            - Set temporary directory (default: $TMPDIR or /tmp)
-automator               - Echo the Automator Quick Action shell script for Finder integration

See INSTALL for installation and macOS permission setup.
